# GitHub works out a repository's language with Linguist, which counts source
# files without caring who wrote them. Two vendored C libraries — liblc3 for
# the glasses' audio and rnnoise for the denoiser — outnumber everything else
# on disk, so the repository was being advertised as a C project. It is Dart,
# and people looking for a Dart or Flutter client filter it out before they
# ever open it.
#
# Marking the vendored trees as such fixes the badge without hiding the code:
# the files stay in the repository, stay in THIRD_PARTY.md, and stay readable.
android/app/src/main/cpp/liblc3/** linguist-vendored
android/app/src/main/cpp/rnnoise/** linguist-vendored
android/app/src/main/cpp/include/** linguist-vendored

# CMake's compiler probes, written by the build rather than by anyone.
android/app/.cxx/** linguist-generated

# The reverse-engineering notes are documentation, not a source file.
*Protocol.txt linguist-documentation
